  "sourcesTitle": "Where our numbers come from",
  "sourcesIntro": "Every target Eatzify sets is computed from published guidance, not invented. These are the sources behind each calculation.",
  "sourcesLink": "Where our numbers come from",
  "sourceBmrTitle": "Resting energy (BMR)",
  "sourceBmrBody": "Mifflin-St Jeor equation. Chosen over Harris-Benedict because it is more accurate in modern populations. We apply no Indian correction factor — the evidence for a single population coefficient is not strong enough — which is why our deficit ceiling is deliberately conservative.",
  "sourceActivityTitle": "Activity multipliers",
  "sourceActivityBody": "Four tiers only: 1.20 sedentary, 1.375 light, 1.55 moderate, 1.725 heavy. We do not offer an athlete tier — self-reported activity is already the largest error in the calculation, and more tiers move that error around rather than reducing it.",
  "sourceIbwTitle": "Ideal and adjusted body weight",
  "sourceIbwBody": "Ideal weight is computed at BMI 23, the Asian/Indian reference, not the 25 used for European populations. Protein is then set on adjusted body weight, which matters most at higher BMI.",
  "sourceProteinTitle": "Protein",
  "sourceProteinBody": "Never below 0.83 g per kg of body weight, the ICMR Recommended Dietary Allowance. Capped at 2.2 g per kg adjusted weight and at 40% of your calories. Reduced further where kidney function may be affected.",
  "sourceFloorsTitle": "Safety floors",
  "sourceFloorsBody": "Daily intake is never planned below 1,500 kcal for men or 1,200 for women, never below your resting energy, and never at a deficit above 750 kcal or 1% of body weight per week. These floors cannot be overridden in the app.",
  "sourceFoodTitle": "Food and nutrition data",
  "sourceFoodBody": "Indian foods are sourced from ICMR-NIN's Indian Food Composition Tables and the Indian Nutrient Databank. Packaged foods come from Open Food Facts, used under the Open Database Licence.",
  "sourcesReviewNote": "Our clinical constants are versioned and reviewed. When a number changes, plans generated before the change keep the numbers they were built with.",
